-- title:
--   Rigid-level valuation ring reads level-M' constant reductions
-- statement:
--   Write $\mathsf q$ for the variable of the Laurent series fields and $\kappa_A$ for the residue field of a valuation subring $A$. Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and $M' \ge 1$ with $q \nmid M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit, and a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` — the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of $\mathbb Q\bigl(j(\mathsf q^{d}) : d \mid M'\bigr)$ — with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, the subfield of $\kappa_A((\mathsf q))$ generated over $\kappa_A$ by the reduced $j$-expansion $\mathsf q^{-1}\cdot(\text{numerator})$ and its substitution $\mathsf q \mapsto \mathsf q^{M'}$; thus $R_0$ consists of a valuation subring of the big field whose constants are exactly $A$, a surjective homomorphism onto that field with kernel the maximal ideal and extending the residue map of $A$, and a degree-preserving map of places compatible with divisors of elements of nonzero residue (these axioms summarised here). Assume moreover that every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral, with $R_0$-residue equal to its coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element of $A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$. Let $\ell'$ be a prime and $K_\ell$ the compositum inside $k_0((\mathsf q))$ of $k_0$ with the coefficientwise image of the level-$(q\ell')^2M'$ function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) for the subgroup $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q * ℓ') M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$; $K_\ell$ is assumed to be an algebra over $A \cap k_0$ compatibly with $k_0$. Let $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ be nonzero with underlying series the coefficientwise image of the $j$-expansion, and assume $j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'}) =$ `jqNModC k₀ (q * ℓ')` lies in $K_\ell$. Let $V$ be a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ such that: an element of $k_0$ lies in $V$ exactly when it comes from $A \cap k_0$; every element of $K_\ell$ integral over $(A \cap k_0)[j_\ell]$ lies in $V$; and for every polynomial $p$ over $A \cap k_0$, if $p$ (with coefficients mapped to $k_0$) evaluated at $j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'})$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$, then all coefficients of $p$ lie in the maximal ideal of $A \cap k_0$. Finally let $g$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$ lying in the full level-$M'$ modular function field, whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral and satisfies $\operatorname{ord}_P(g) \ge 0$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\operatorname{ord}_P(j) \ge 0$, and assume $g(\mathsf q^{\ell'})$ lies in $K_\ell$. Then $g(\mathsf q^{\ell'})$ lies in $V$, and it lies in the maximal ideal of $V$ if and only if the $R_0$-residue of the image of $g$ vanishes in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`.
--
--   This is the Igusa-type comparison asserting that a valuation ring of the rigid-level function field attached to $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$, pinned down by its constants, its finite chart algebra and the residual transcendence of the moduli invariant $j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'})$, computes the reduction of level-$M'$ modular functions through the constant reduction $R_0$. It supplies the level-$M'$ law used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelLaws_trace_of_igusaBranch_of_rigidChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelLaws_trace_of_igusaBranch_of_rigidChart) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.pernodeConclusion_traces_of_rigidDescentHyps`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.pernodeConclusion_traces_of_rigidDescentHyps).
